sh <scriptname.sh> - to run Shell files

crontab - scheduler
eg: crontab -e -> to open cron tab editor and  * * * * * echo "Hello world from crontab"

crontab - l -> to list output
* * * * * ->  min hour day month weekday(0-6)

sudo tail -f /var/log/cron - to check crontab logs


eg: crontab -e -> to open cron tab editor and  * * * * * sh /home/ec2-user/shell-practice/5_Shell.sh
sudo tail -f /var/log/cron - to check crontab logs of that script



Notes2:
ShellScripting:
Shell has three types - bash, zsh, ksh
#!/bin/bash - shebang - uses bash interpreter

Git:
git init - to intialize git repo
git config --local user.name "name"/git config --global user.name "name"
git config --local user.email "email"/git config --global user.email "email"
git add .
git commit -m "commit"
git status
git remote add origin <repo url>
git push origin master
git pull

git log
git revert <commit-id>
git branch <branchname>, eg: git branch develop
git branch  - list branches
git checkout -b develop - to create and switch to develop branch
git checkout <commitid> - to check to that commit change
git merge develop - enter this from master branch to merge develop branch to main branch
git branch -d develop - delete the develop branch if not needed as it is merged to main branch

Use the PAT Token for HTTPS Authentication:
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/repository.git
Username: your GitHub username
Password: [Paste your Personal Access Token]

we can also use SSH or git cli Authentication methods.

